<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="67703" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/IS/390/67703.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="IS" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/IS.xml">Information Sciences</subject><course id="390" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/IS/390.xml">Special Topics in Information Studies</course></parents><sectionNumber>BS </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Blockchain and Society</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course examines blockchain and decentralized technologies through both a technical and social lens. Topics include the introduction and evolution of blockchain networks, consensus mechanisms used to facilitate transactions, smart contracts and decentralized applications, and the implications of governance models. No special skills or prerequisite knowledge are needed as the course also covers the technical specifics needed to implement blockchain systems.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>10:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>134</roomNumber><buildingName>Armory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Rusch" firstName="A">Rusch, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>